{"path":"std/fs/fn.write.html","title":"Function write","description":"Writes a slice as the entire contents of a file.","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"anchor","id":"main-content"},{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Function write"}]},{"type":"text","value":"1.26.0 · "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/src/std/fs.rs.html#420-425","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"pub fn write<P: AsRef<Path>, C: AsRef<[u8]>>(path: P, contents: C) -> Result<()>"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Writes a slice as the entire contents of a file."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function will create a file if it does not exist, and will entirely replace its contents if it does."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Depending on the platform, this function may fail if the full directory path does not exist."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is a convenience function for using "},{"type":"link","href":"std/fs/struct.File.html#method.create","title":"associated function std::fs::File::create","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"File::create"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/io/trait.Write.html#method.write_all","title":"method std::io::Write::write_all","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"write_all"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with fewer imports."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"use std::fs;\n\nfn main() -> std::io::Result<()> {\n    fs::write(\"foo.txt\", b\"Lorem ipsum\")?;\n    fs::write(\"bar.txt\", \"dolor sit\")?;\n    Ok(())\n}"},{"type":"link","href":"https://play.rust-lang.org/?code=%23!%5Ballow(unused)%5D%0Ause+std::fs;%0A%0Afn+main()+-%3E+std::io::Result%3C()%3E